>
  <p>Stuck at a keypad or a safe? Here's every GTA 6 code found since launch. The first two tables list codes that at least two independent sources agree on. Codes from a single source are at the bottom, so treat those as "try it".</p>
  <div class="callout"><p><strong>Robbery safes may be random.</strong> Story and puzzle codes are fixed. Safes in random store robberies are reported to change per save. Look for a note on the premises, check a guard, or aim at an employee and use the <strong>Safe Code?</strong> prompt.</p></div>

  <h2>Story mission codes</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>Mission</th><th>Code</th><th>Opens</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{table(story).map(([w, m, c, o]) => <tr><td>{w}</td><td>{m}</td><td><strong>{c}</strong></td><td>{o}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p><small>Some outlets call 0420 the "Moonstone Boutique room" code rather than the acid lab door. It's the same code.</small></p>

  <h2>Free roam and gang hideout codes</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>Type</th><th>Code</th><th>Opens</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{table(freeRoam).map(([w, m, c, o]) => <tr><td>{w}</td><td>{m}</td><td><strong>{c}</strong></td><td>{o}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p><small>The three gang hideout codes are revealed by the wall map inside Brooks Boatworks. Hideout codes may vary per save.</small></p>
  <p><strong>The Vamos garage (2727):</strong> Moses's job sends you to a property in Grayson where the '74 Declasse Vamos sits in a locked garage with a keypad. We searched the house and the grounds and couldn't spot a clue. Guides say the number is on a license plate or a flag sticker inside the trailer next to the garage. You don't need it: type <strong>2727</strong> and the door opens (tested on our stream). To skip the long drive to Moses, see the <a href="/gta-6/make-money/#moses-delivery-trick">car delivery trick</a>.</p>

  <h2>Crab research outpost walkthrough (CLEAVES, 0072, 0212)</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Go to the abandoned outpost in the southwest of the Pelican Valley swamps, just north of the Keys.</li>
    <li>Flip the power switch on the outside of the main house.</li>
    <li>In a side room, examine the writing on the floor: the computer password is <strong>CLEAVES</strong>.</li>
    <li>The computer hints the safe is <strong>"double success"</strong>. The lab notes call specimen <strong>0036</strong> the major breakthrough, so the safe is <strong>0072</strong>.</li>
    <li>The safe holds about $1,000 and the boathouse code <strong>0212</strong>. The boathouse at the end of the dock has the unique <strong>Crabshack VF5 SMG</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The orange SCOOP container in the yard needs the Cut-off Tool from a later story mission, so skip it on your first visit.</p>

  <h2>Reported by one source (unconfirmed)</h2>
  <div class="table-scroll"><table>
    <thead><tr><th>Where</th><th>Type</th><th>Code</th><th>Opens</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>{table(single).map(([w, m, c, o]) => <tr><td>{w}</td><td>{m}</td><td><strong>{c}</strong></td><td>{o}</td></tr>)}</tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p><small>Mount Kalaga's firewatch tower shed is reported as both 69185 and 691865, so neither is confirmed yet. Janjak's Garage hasn't been found. We move codes up once a second source confirms them.</small></p>

  <p>Planning a bigger score? See <a href="/gta-6/heists/">what we know about GTA 6 heists</a> and the <a href="/gta-6/cheat-codes/">GTA 6 cheat codes</a>.</p>
